# ScrollBench Test Application - Implementation Plan

## Goal

Create an isolated test application to validate viewport culling and frame budget optimizations for efficiently handling 10,000+ image thumbnails without blocking the UI thread.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Testing Approach**: This is a separate test application. Manual verification will involve:
> 1. Running the app with 10,000 generated test images
> 2. Monitoring FPS overlay while scrolling
> 3. Observing main thread responsiveness
> 4. Comparing metrics with/without optimizations enabled
>
> Do you have a preferred test image dataset, or should I generate synthetic test data using colored rectangles with metadata?

## Proposed Changes

### Component 1: Build System

#### [NEW] [test_scrollbench/CMakeLists.txt](file:///d:/Dev/antigravity/test_scrollbench/CMakeLists.txt)

- New CMake configuration for `appScrollBench` executable
- Links to existing dependencies: Qt6::Quick, Qt6::Concurrent, Qt6::Gui
